# Live data snapshots contain the PT's real client data — never commit.
# THIS REPO IS PUBLIC. Preserve anything that must survive to
# C:\projects\_archive\PTApp\ (outside the repo), never to a tracked path.
#
# tmp/ is ignored WHOLESALE (2026-08-03). The old narrow patterns below only
# matched *-snapshot.json, and tmp/ was in fact holding two full live-data
# exports (post-recovery.json, ptapp-live-20260511.json) that neither pattern
# caught — one `git add -A` from publishing real client names and phone
# numbers. tmp/ is wipeable scratch by convention, so nothing in it should
# ever be committed; a directory-wide ignore is the only rule that can't be
# out-run by a new filename.
tmp/

# Sanity scripts moved tmp/ → scripts/sanity/ in v2.9.3 (Apr 21 2026);
# that directory IS tracked, so snapshots dropped there still need patterns.
scripts/sanity/live-snapshot-*.json
scripts/sanity/*-snapshot.json
scripts/sanity/*-data.json
